   "design": "A record query built from the protocol's inclusion and exclusion criteria lists candidate patients ({OTHER}), so the internist does not page through records; the internist confirms each one. Lab values, vital signs and medication flow from the record into the study's electronic forms ({DATA_PLATFORM}), and the internist adds only study-specific observations. Informing patients, treating them and judging results stay with the internist.",
   "previous_blocker": "Candidates were found by reading records and data copied by hand into study forms.",
   "enabler_now": "Record queries find candidates; study forms can import record data.",
   "still_hard": "Criteria in free text do not fit a query.",
   "human_edge": "Explaining a study honestly so a patient can say no.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "The internist confirms candidates and data instead of searching and copying.",
